        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi, Nikita!\r\n\r\nThanks for using 'mini.files'!\r\n\r\n> I was wondering if adding an option to automatically display line numbers for mini.files buffers was possible. I believe that it would make navigation easier.\r\n\r\nIt is already possible. Customizing windows is expected to be done inside [dedicated events](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e025ee74705b04dd25a132a521c9c535dc78a8d8/doc/mini-files.txt#L323-L327). Here is an [example from help page](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e025ee74705b04dd25a132a521c9c535dc78a8d8/doc/mini-files.txt#L368-L381). Note that 'number' window option is a bit special (it is disabled on every window update due to `'minimal'` style of floating windows), so it should be set in every `MiniFilesWindowUpdate` event and not `MiniFilesWindowOpen`.\r\n\r\nHere is an example of full working config:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.files').setup()\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\r\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesWindowUpdate',\r\n  callback = function(args) vim.wo[args.data.win_id].number = true end,\r\n})\r\n```",
