            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should be now resolved on latest `main` branch.\r\n\r\nThe reason for this was quite technical: `MiniFilesWindowUpdate` event was triggered *before* window got its target buffer assigned to it. Which was not good, so thanks for inadvertently finding this!\r\n\r\nAs 'number' is a window-local option (which are notoriously convoluted as to how they work), it got overridden after buffer was assigned to the window. But now (when event gets triggered *after* window gets its buffer) setup from [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/747#issuecomment-1995360187) seems to work for me completely.",
